{"title":"2015 USAJMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given a sequence of real numbers, a move consists of choosing two terms and replacing each with their arithmetic mean. Show that there exists a sequence of 2015 distinct real numbers such that after one initial move is applied to the sequence -- no matter what move -- there is always a way to continue with a finite sequence of moves so as to obtain in the end a constant sequence.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solve in integers the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a563dd59e15d5c2022ae9f69c6be35c042bec806.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+xy+y^2 = \\left(\\frac{x+y}{3}+1\\right)^3.\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21363140fbe1a1f51c21f6c4731f1d56dd9a650d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APBQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac80bc77394a33c3e18143e17c43d1b261ab1ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P = \\angle Q = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86baca28012c300e13ead6015a3b9f2bd8a75953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AQ &lt; BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a variable point on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> (other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />). Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cc35adb36da24d8436f0d49b7cdb3065061d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e8571374bd200b0a9b5331e9501145c838c806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XT}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba52c969bed0d101e945b960e9e2b96604fcadb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AX}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> denote the midpoint of chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c79d1720945ed79ebd44d6bf48bba9ba3e5bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ST}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> varies on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" />, show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> moves along a circle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d14be9ef31fb5c791a4f795a8bd131aa5aeecb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{Q}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{Q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ecb395c1e56e6d9726fc45f1bc7a66d98333da2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)+f(t)=f(y)+f(z)\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"18\" />for all rational numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210be37dd4eb992da14968d95ba23b1fedbcd30b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;y&lt;z&lt;t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> that form an arithmetic progression. (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18faac56812975e05744319e3c6ac1016643c11b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> is the set of all rational numbers.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral. Prove that there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e3cf63362076edf83dde3193fc697a27500f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=\\angle XAD$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8ab3681c0077ec0700f1d60eee66bfebd91417d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA=\\angle XCD$\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" /> if and only if there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c0f3d89c0cf19444eccaabc5d71370148965f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBD=\\angle YBA$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac55835de7e220eafe5fbba5846da55bf66e7d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDB=\\angle YDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Steve is piling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99c85dd00eb11d60bb8d0332530445cf25c5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> indistinguishable stones on the squares of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> grid. Each square can have an arbitrarily high pile of stones. After he finished piling his stones in some manner, he can then perform stone moves, defined as follows. Consider any four grid squares, which are corners of a rectangle, i.e. in positions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0b533f1c1f3a68bacf9f4856b83f67898aaa73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, k), (i, l), (j, k), (j, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d3d6c286899a6607c08c5c500816d1bf70f345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i, j, k, l\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8b76bca5358138116d4d962e20e582bfa708b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20ccf57f7714b83f64a8ef7e1bd9e18ccfbe78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;l$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />. A stone move consists of either removing one stone from each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec83d11312e52717655024b28bbde1050b97198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e579d3552c24aaaccbc4559c92f9291e6e69d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> and moving them to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea35c25b8931e32f87157fd76853f9200902acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472226e072e2a15cf4e76b655a5b11bd1bce21f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> respectively, or removing one stone from each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea35c25b8931e32f87157fd76853f9200902acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472226e072e2a15cf4e76b655a5b11bd1bce21f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and moving them to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec83d11312e52717655024b28bbde1050b97198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e579d3552c24aaaccbc4559c92f9291e6e69d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Two ways of piling the stones are equivalent if they can be obtained from one another by a sequence of stone moves.\n</p><p>How many different non-equivalent ways can Steve pile the stones on the grid?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\">USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO\" title=\"2015 USAJMO\">2015 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2014 USAJMO Problems\">2014 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems\">2016 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060900\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.066 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 301/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 84/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8418/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.343      1 -total\n 51.47%    7.382      1 Template:USAJMO_box\n 46.24%    6.632      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14190:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060900 and revision id 196450. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}